  "outcome": {
    "ok": true,
    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r5:t4",
    "narration": "The floor held the stillness of a space that had been empty for a long time and was only now being inhabited again. Two beds with their bare frames, two stools, two nightstands, two wardrobes standing open and hollow — all of it faced inward as though waiting for purpose that had not yet arrived. The wooden cabinets opposite caught the thin light from the perimeter windows, their shelves clean and unlabeled. The spiral stair curved away at the edge of the floor, its opening a quiet interruption in the otherwise open room.\n\nIris sat on one of the stools, near but not at the bedside. She had been still through the last exchanges, her hands resting in her lap. The quiet had settled between them without strain. When it stretched long enough to feel like a thing chosen rather than merely left, she shifted her weight slightly and looked toward the windows.\n\n\"I don't mind either,\" she said. \"But if you're asking, the view.\"",
